# 8. AUTOMATIC PENDING QUESTION CARRY-FORWARD

This feature must work independently for every account.

Example:

Day 1:
- Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5 assigned.
- Q1 and Q2 completed.
- Q3, Q4 and Q5 pending.

Day 2:
- Q3, Q4 and Q5 appear automatically.
- No new questions are added until the pending workload is cleared.

Once pending work is cleared, the system can assign five new questions from the same active topic.

Rules:

- Preserve original assignment dates.
- Show Pending labels.
- Never delete unfinished work.
- Never mark unfinished work as solved.
- Never silently replace pending questions.
- Preserve original problem URLs.
- Carry forward until manually completed.
- Never mix another user's assignments.

If the user has more than five pending questions, display all of them.

